infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title JSONB vs typed column: who is the source of the demand?
  desc Schema drives variability → JSONB. Query drives the demand → typed column.
  compares
    - label JSONB column
      children
        - label Heterogeneous data
          desc Event payloads, third-party API shapes, per-tenant config
        - label Long-tail metadata
          desc 80% share 10 columns, 20% carry a 50-field tail
        - label Read as a unit
          desc Stored but rarely queried by field — read the whole row
    - label Typed column
      children
        - label Appears in WHERE / GROUP BY
          desc Anything you filter, sort, or aggregate on
        - label JOIN or foreign key
          desc Referenced across tables — needs integrity
        - label UNIQUE or CHECK
          desc Constraints the engine must enforce per row
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
